.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_QUERY_ONE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_query_one \- look up a single-valued query parameter
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_req_query_one(chttpsvr_req *req,
                                      const char *key,
                                      const char **val_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Looks up a query parameter that must appear exactly once, matching
key against the URL-decoded keys of the query string exactly as
chttpsvr_req_query does.  Unlike chttpsvr_req_query, this function
distinguishes an out-of-memory failure from an absent key, and it
allocates no scratch array for the result.

On any failure it sets *val_out to NULL, provided that val_out itself
is not NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success; exactly one value was found and stored in *val_out.
ccol_key_not_found; the key is absent.
ccol_not_permitted; the key appears more than once.
ccol_not_enough_memory; the parse buffer for the query string could
not be allocated.
ccol_invalid_args; req or key is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_query (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_query_oom (3)
